WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.980
A five metre ladder leans against a wall.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.880
Someone walks its foot out along
the floor at a steady pace.

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.450
A marker on the wall tracks the top.

4
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.630
At first it creeps down.

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:14.090
Near the floor, it plunges.

6
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:17.590
The foot moves steadily,
and gravity plays no part.

7
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:20.080
So why does the top speed up?

8
00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:25.150
In this mission, you'll see the ladder,
wall and floor as a right-angled triangle:

9
00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.610
x squared plus y squared
equals twenty five.

10
00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:33.130
Both x and y change with time, so you'll
differentiate the equation that links

11
00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:35.180
them with respect to t.

12
00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: explain why the ladder's
top speeds up as it nears the floor.
